---
/** /widebeam SOUND key (lane A), position: fixed; placed by furniture.ts. Its name is its visible text, a fixed "Sound"
 *  (no aria-label, a11y-11 / demo-12), and aria-pressed carries the state, with the EQ bars as its lamp (still when
 *  off, moving when on). A label that flipped "Sound off" / "Sound on" said the state twice and read as the action
 *  (WAI-ARIA toggle pattern: the name stays fixed, r-asks-soundname). sound.ts (lane D) owns the click and aria-pressed
 *  and never writes its text. On phones it is a 44 px round
 *  key: the text is clipped visually, never display:none, so it stays the name. */
---
<button type="button" class="wb-sound" data-wb-sound data-wb-demo aria-pressed="false"><span class="wb-eq" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="wb-sound-face">Sound</span></button>
